# Read fumadocs-ui's hard-coded English accessible names from its i18n context.
#
# WHY THIS PIN EXISTS
# -------------------
# fumadocs-ui 16.8.12 writes nine accessible names as English literals inside
# its components, outside its own Translations API, so no `translations` passed
# to `RootProvider` can reach them. Every locale page served them in English
# inside `<html lang="de">`, `<html lang="ja">`, ... (#305, a WCAG 3.1.2
# language-of-parts defect). Measured on the built pages of `main` at cec227a,
# per locale (82 pages each; the seven locales agree to within 12):
#
#   aria-label="Copy Anchor Link"   692-699   components/heading.js
#   aria-label="Copy Text"          201-206   components/codeblock.js
#   aria-label="Open Search"            160   layouts/shared/slots/search-trigger.js
#   aria-label="Collapse Sidebar"       158   components/sidebar/base.js
#   aria-label="Toggle Theme"            81   layouts/shared/slots/theme-switch.js
#   aria-label="Open Sidebar"            79   components/sidebar/base.js
#   aria-label="Toggle Menu"              2   layouts/home/slots/header.js
#   aria-label="Main"                     2   layouts/home/slots/header.js (Radix)
#
# plus two that only exist after interaction and so are not in prerendered
# HTML: "Copied Text" (a code block's copy button, after a click) and the
# drawer's own "Open Sidebar" (rendered client-side below 768px).
#
# WHAT THIS CHANGES
# -----------------
# Nine keys join `defaultTranslations` (contexts/i18n.js) and the
# `Translations` interface (contexts/i18n.d.ts), each defaulting to the exact
# English literal it replaces; each component reads its name from
# `useI18n().text`. `I18nProvider` already spreads the `translations` it is
# given over the defaults, so `apps/docs/lib/ui-text.ts` supplies the nine
# strings through the same `RootProvider` prop as the other ten. With no
# provider, or a provider that omits a key, the name is the old English
# literal: English renders byte-identically.
#
# Eight of the keys are a BACKPORT of upstream's own fix. fumadocs-ui 16.9.0
# (the next minor after this pin) ships exactly these names, with these
# defaults, in the same flat Translations object: `searchOpen`, `themeToggle`,
# `sidebarOpen`, `sidebarCollapse`, `headingCopyAnchor`, `codeBlockCopy`,
# `codeBlockCopied`, `menuToggle`. Measured 2026-10-06 by unpacking the
# published 16.9.0 tarball: its `dist/i18n.js` declares them and its
# components read `t.searchOpen` and so on where 16.8.12 has literals.
#
# The ninth, `navMain`, is NOT upstream. Radix's NavigationMenu root defaults
# `aria-label="Main"`, and fumadocs' HomeLayout header (the privacy and terms
# pages here) renders that root without a label of its own. Upstream still
# passes none in 16.16.2 (latest on 2026-10-06), so this hunk has nothing to
# track and is the one to re-check on any bump.
#
# WHY A PATCH AND NOT SLOT OVERRIDES
# ----------------------------------
# Each name was checked against the DocsLayout / HomeLayout slot API first.
# None is reachable in every place it renders without re-implementing the
# component that renders it:
#
# - "Open Search": `slots.searchTrigger.sm` covers the mobile header, but the
#   collapsed-sidebar panel imports `SearchTrigger` directly.
# - "Collapse Sidebar" (both instances) and the drawer's "Open Sidebar" are
#   rendered inside the docs `Sidebar` slot itself; the only override is
#   replacing `slots.sidebar.root`, a ~200-line fork of fumadocs' sidebar.
# - "Toggle Theme": `slots.themeSwitch` replaces the whole switch; the label is
#   not a prop of the stock one.
# - "Copy Anchor Link" / "Copy Text": the MDX `h1`-`h6` and `pre` components
#   would have to be re-implemented; neither copy button takes a label.
# - "Toggle Menu" / "Main": only `slots.header` (all of the HomeLayout header).
#
# The one name an override could have reached cleanly, the header's sidebar
# button (`slots.sidebar.trigger` accepts `aria-label`), is the same component
# as the drawer's, so the patch has to change it anyway; an override on top
# would be dead code. One mechanism, in the components that own the names,
# reading the context those components already read for `text.search`.
#
# Not covered, because nothing on this site renders them: `bannerClose`
# (Banner), `accordionCopyAnchor` (Accordion), the light/dark/system labels of
# ThemeSwitch's `light-dark-system` mode, `layouts/shared/page-actions.js` (the
# app has its own, localized), the Orama/Algolia dialog footers, and
# `layouts/home/not-found.js` (the app has `app/not-found.tsx`).
#
# WHEN THIS FILE CAN BE DELETED
# -----------------------------
# On the upgrade to fumadocs-ui 16.9.0 or later. Delete this file and its
# `pnpm.patchedDependencies` entry in the root `package.json`, re-run
# `pnpm install`, then move `navMain` to whatever that version offers (nothing,
# as of 16.16.2: it would need re-patching or a `slots.header` override).
# 16.10.0 and later replace the flat Translations object with string-keyed
# `t("Open Search")` lookups, so on those `lib/ui-text.ts` changes shape too.
#
# What makes a silent loss loud: `fumadocsTranslations()` in
# `apps/docs/lib/ui-text.ts` returns an object literal typed as fumadocs'
# `Translations`; on a version whose `Translations` lacks these keys that is an
# excess-property error and `tsc` fails `type-check`. And as with the
# fumadocs-core pin beside this one, a bump of the package without
# regenerating this file fails `pnpm install` with ERR_PNPM_UNUSED_PATCH.
#
